---
import Footer from "../components/Footer.astro";
import Header from "../components/Header.astro";
import {
  NODE_FLOOR,
  PRODUCT_VERSION,
  PROFILE_COUNT,
  PROVIDER_COUNT,
  SOURCE_SHA,
  WORKFLOWS,
} from "../data/product";
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
---

<Base title="librarium | Evidence-aware, multi-provider research">
  <Header />

  <main>
    <section class="border-b border-neutral-950/10 py-16 sm:py-24">
      <div class="mx-auto grid max-w-6xl grid-cols-1 items-center gap-12 px-6 lg:grid-cols-[11fr_9fr] lg:px-8">
        <div>
          <p class="font-mono text-sm font-medium tracking-wide text-amber-700 uppercase sm:text-xs">
            Open source · MIT · v2 release candidate
          </p>
          <h1 class="mt-5 max-w-[22ch] text-5xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-balance text-neutral-950 sm:text-6xl">
            Research across providers. Keep the evidence boundaries.
          </h1>
          <p class="mt-6 max-w-[58ch] text-lg text-pretty text-neutral-600">
            Librarium plans one request against explicit provider profiles, runs the selected work, and records what happened. Use it for web search, cited answers, consumer-surface observations, and durable research jobs.
          </p>
          <div class="mt-9 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-4">
            <a href="/docs" class="rounded-lg bg-neutral-950 px-4 py-2.5 text-base font-medium text-white hover:bg-neutral-800 focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-amber-600 sm:text-sm">
              Evaluate v2
            </a>
            <a href="https://github.com/jkudish/librarium" class="rounded-lg px-4 py-2.5 text-base font-medium text-neutral-700 ring-1 ring-neutral-950/15 hover:bg-neutral-950/3 sm:text-sm">
              Read the source
            </a>
          </div>
          <div class="mt-7 flex max-w-xl flex-col items-start justify-between gap-3 rounded-lg bg-neutral-950/3 p-3 ring-1 ring-neutral-950/10 sm:flex-row sm:items-center sm:py-2 sm:pr-2 sm:pl-4">
            <p class="font-mono text-base text-neutral-800 sm:text-sm">RC18 review is pinned to source {SOURCE_SHA.slice(0, 12)}</p>
            <a href="/docs/release-candidate" class="shrink-0 rounded-md bg-white px-2.5 py-1 font-mono text-sm font-medium text-neutral-600 ring-1 ring-neutral-950/10 hover:text-neutral-950 focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-amber-600 sm:text-xs">
              build from source
            </a>
          </div>
          <p class="mt-4 text-base/7 text-pretty text-neutral-500 sm:text-sm/6">
            RC18 is not available from npm, Homebrew, or standalone release channels. Its source build requires Node.js {NODE_FLOOR} or newer.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="overflow-hidden rounded-xl bg-neutral-950 shadow-lg ring-1 ring-neutral-950/10">
          <div class="flex flex-col items-start gap-1 border-b border-white/10 px-5 py-3 sm:flex-row sm:items-center sm:justify-between sm:gap-3">
            <p class="font-mono text-sm text-neutral-400 sm:text-xs">offline canonical fixture replay</p>
            <p class="font-mono text-sm text-amber-300 sm:text-xs">network denied</p>
          </div>
          <div class="p-5 font-mono text-sm/6 text-neutral-300">
            <pre class="whitespace-pre-wrap break-words"><code><span class="text-neutral-500">$ </span>librarium live-validation \
  --fixture /absolute/path/to/fixture.json

&#123;
  <span class="text-sky-300">"status"</span>: <span class="text-emerald-300">"succeeded"</span>,
  <span class="text-sky-300">"schema_version"</span>: 1,
  <span class="text-sky-300">"artifact_name"</span>: <span class="text-amber-300">"run_manifest"</span>,
  <span class="text-sky-300">"request_id"</span>: <span class="text-amber-300">"fixture-readme-durable-replay"</span>,
  <span class="text-sky-300">"profile"</span>: <span class="text-amber-300">"exa/research"</span>,
  <span class="text-sky-300">"binding_id"</span>: <span class="text-amber-300">"exa.research.exa-research"</span>,
  <span class="text-sky-300">"materialize_count"</span>: 1,
  <span class="text-sky-300">"resume_count"</span>: 1,
  <span class="text-sky-300">"submit_count"</span>: 1,
  <span class="text-sky-300">"poll_count"</span>: 1,
  <span class="text-sky-300">"retrieve_count"</span>: 1
&#125;</code></pre>
          </div>
          <p class="border-t border-white/10 px-5 py-3 text-base/7 text-pretty text-neutral-400 sm:text-sm/6">
            This is the reviewed, network-denied fixture path. It does not claim live provider behavior, account state, price, or privacy settings. <a href="/demo.gif" class="font-medium text-amber-300 hover:text-amber-200">Watch the source replay</a>.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="py-16 sm:py-24" id="workflows">
      <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-6 lg:px-8">
        <p class="font-mono text-sm font-medium tracking-wide text-amber-700 uppercase sm:text-xs">V2 catalog</p>
        <h2 class="mt-4 max-w-[32ch] text-4xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-balance text-neutral-950">
          Profiles are the public unit of selection and provenance.
        </h2>
        <p class="mt-5 max-w-[70ch] text-base/7 text-pretty text-neutral-600">
          The catalog has {PROVIDER_COUNT} built-in providers and {PROFILE_COUNT} implemented public profiles. Select a profile as <code class="rounded bg-neutral-950/4 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-neutral-950">provider_id/profile_id</code>. Internal adapter IDs are not public configuration.
        </p>
        <dl class="mt-12 grid grid-cols-1 gap-8 sm:grid-cols-2">
          {WORKFLOWS.map((workflow) => (
            <div class="rounded-xl border border-neutral-950/10 p-6">
              <dt class="font-mono text-base font-medium text-neutral-950 sm:text-sm">{workflow.id}</dt>
              <dd class="mt-3 text-base/7 text-pretty text-neutral-600 sm:text-sm/6">{workflow.summary}</dd>
              {workflow.selection[0] !== "catalog-derived" && (
                <dd class="mt-4 font-mono text-base/7 text-pretty text-neutral-600 sm:text-sm/6">
                  {workflow.selection.join(" · ")}
                </dd>
              )}
            </div>
          ))}
        </dl>
        <p class="mt-8 text-base/7 text-pretty text-neutral-500 sm:text-sm/6">
          These are the only four built-in v2 workflows. User-authored groups use <code class="font-mono">custom:&lt;name&gt;</code>.{" "}
          <a href="/docs/groups-and-modes" class="font-medium text-amber-700 hover:text-amber-600">Read the workflow contract</a>.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="border-y border-neutral-950/10 bg-neutral-950/2 py-16 sm:py-24" id="evidence">
      <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-6 lg:px-8">
        <p class="font-mono text-sm font-medium tracking-wide text-amber-700 uppercase sm:text-xs">Evidence, not a confidence score</p>
        <h2 class="mt-4 max-w-[35ch] text-4xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-balance text-neutral-950">
          Preserve what each result can and cannot establish.
        </h2>
        <div class="mt-12 grid grid-cols-1 gap-8 lg:grid-cols-3">
          <div class="border-t border-neutral-950/10 pt-6">
            <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-neutral-950">API output</h3>
            <p class="mt-3 text-base/7 text-pretty text-neutral-600 sm:text-sm/6">
              A direct API response records what the named API returned. Provider-reported citations, usage, and cost remain labelled as reported facts, not Librarium estimates.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="border-t border-neutral-950/10 pt-6">
            <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-neutral-950">Collected surfaces</h3>
            <p class="mt-3 text-base/7 text-pretty text-neutral-600 sm:text-sm/6">
              Six SearchAPI profiles observe consumer surfaces through one collector. Their agreement is correlated visibility evidence, not six independent confirmations or parity with a specific user.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="border-t border-neutral-950/10 pt-6">
            <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-neutral-950">Corpus provenance</h3>
            <p class="mt-3 text-base/7 text-pretty text-neutral-600 sm:text-sm/6">
              Web, X-only, combined web and X, and specialized sources keep distinct profile identities. Shared URLs show overlap. They do not prove independent corroboration.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <a href="/docs/output-formats#provenance-is-descriptive" class="mt-8 inline-flex text-base font-medium text-amber-700 hover:text-amber-600 sm:text-sm">
          Read the provenance model
        </a>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="py-16 sm:py-24" id="library">
      <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-6 lg:px-8">
        <p class="font-mono text-sm font-medium tracking-wide text-amber-700 uppercase sm:text-xs">Three package boundaries</p>
        <h2 class="mt-4 max-w-[33ch] text-4xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-balance text-neutral-950">
          Import only the runtime responsibilities you own.
        </h2>
        <div class="mt-12 grid grid-cols-1 gap-8 lg:grid-cols-3">
          <div class="rounded-xl border border-neutral-950/10 p-6">
            <h3 class="font-mono text-base font-medium text-neutral-950 sm:text-sm">librarium</h3>
            <p class="mt-3 text-base/7 text-pretty text-neutral-600 sm:text-sm/6">Side-effect-free schemas, config migration, and the public catalog. Worker-safe.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="rounded-xl border border-neutral-950/10 p-6">
            <h3 class="font-mono text-base font-medium text-neutral-950 sm:text-sm">librarium/core</h3>
            <p class="mt-3 text-base/7 text-pretty text-neutral-600 sm:text-sm/6">Injected catalog, planning, transport, coordination, and execution ports. It does not construct provider adapters or a global registry.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="rounded-xl border border-neutral-950/10 p-6">
            <h3 class="font-mono text-base font-medium text-neutral-950 sm:text-sm">librarium/node</h3>
            <p class="mt-3 text-base/7 text-pretty text-neutral-600 sm:text-sm/6">Explicit config-file services, trusted custom-provider loading, and canonical validation helpers. The CLI remains the complete Node application.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <p class="mt-8 max-w-[72ch] text-base/7 text-pretty text-neutral-500 sm:text-sm/6">
          MCP, the agent skill, and the Amp plugin expose the same research jobs without pretending that Node persistence and the shared TypeScript/PHP terminal contract are the same architecture.{" "}
          <a href="/docs/library" class="font-medium text-amber-700 hover:text-amber-600">Choose an import boundary</a>.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="pb-16 sm:pb-24" id="review">
      <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-6 lg:px-8">
        <div class="rounded-xl border border-neutral-950/10 bg-neutral-950/2 p-8 sm:p-12">
          <p class="font-mono text-sm font-medium text-amber-700 sm:text-xs">{PRODUCT_VERSION}</p>
          <h2 class="mt-4 max-w-[28ch] text-4xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-balance text-neutral-950">
            Evaluate the release candidate without treating it as released.
          </h2>
          <p class="mt-5 max-w-[66ch] text-base/7 text-pretty text-neutral-600">
            The site facts are pinned to source commit <code class="font-mono text-sm text-neutral-950">{SOURCE_SHA.slice(0, 12)}</code>. Build that exact checkout, inspect the catalog, and run the network-denied fixture. Live provider validation remains a separate paid-call gate.
          </p>
          <div class="mt-8 flex flex-wrap gap-4">
            <a href="/docs/release-candidate" class="rounded-lg bg-neutral-950 px-4 py-2.5 text-base font-medium text-white hover:bg-neutral-800 sm:text-sm">Review the RC checklist</a>
            <a href="/docs/providers" class="rounded-lg px-4 py-2.5 text-base font-medium text-neutral-700 ring-1 ring-neutral-950/15 hover:bg-white sm:text-sm">Inspect all profiles</a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>

  <Footer />
</Base>
